2026-04-04 19:57:16.306 | 1653284 (1653284) | DEBUG    | Model response tool call: {"tool_name": "exit_plan_mode", "args": {"plan": "# HUD Panels Robustness Refactoring Plan\n\nThis plan hardens the core workspace HUDs (`ProjectSettings`, `TemplateLibrary`, `Library`, and `Export`) using defensive programming and Next.js 15 best practices.\n\n## 1. ProjectSettingsHUD.tsx Hardening\n- **Hook Placement**: Consolidate all hooks (`useForm`, `useEffect`) at the top of the component.\n- **Defensive State**: Wrap the `onBlur` update logic in `try-catch` and add an early return for `!project` after hook definitions.\n- **Validation**: Ensure form values are validated before calling `updateProject`.\n\n## 2. TemplateLibraryHUD.tsx Hardening\n- **Safe Materialization**: Wrap the template-to-project conversion logic (parsing TOC markdown) in a `try-catch` block.\n- **Atomic Updates**: Ensure the project structure is updated in a single pass within the `updateProject` callback.\n- **Error States**: Handle potential parsing failures during template application with graceful fallbacks.\n\n## 3. LibraryHUD.tsx Resilience\n- **Safe Loading**: Wrap `handleLoadProject` in a `try-catch` block and provide feedback if navigation or hydration fails.\n- **Navigation Guard**: Add defensive checks to ensure the target project exists before attempting to load or push to `/builder`.\n\n## 4. ExportHUD.tsx Production Hardening\n- **Correct Hook Pattern**: Replace the `useMemo` initialization logic with a proper `useEffect` for syncing selection state.\n- **Safe Compilation**: Wrap `handleExportClick` in `try-catch` to handle potential exporter failures.\n- **Validation**: Ensure selection set size and format types are validated before triggering the production pipeline.\n"}, "tool_call_id": "pyd_ai_8a6059bad1e640a19bb3aba7313f6c94", "id": null, "provider_name": "google-vertex", "provider_details": {"thought_signature": ""}, "part_kind": "tool-call"}
