\\" footers.\\n*   **State**: Zustand for document orchestration; TanStack Query for server-side metadata.\\n*   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RAG & Infrastructure","find":"---\\n\\n## Coding Conventions\\n*   **TypeScript**: Zero tolerance for `any`. Use `unknown` with narrowing.\\n*   **Components**: Default to Server Components; use `\'use client\'` only when necessary.\\n*   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS only. Use `cn()` for merging classes and CVA for variants.\\n*   **State**: Zustand for complex client UI; TanStack Query for server state.\\n*   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts` to ensure consistent status codes and telemetry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RAG & Infrastructure","file_path":"AGENTS.md"}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: find_and_replace_code', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span', 'original_content': '# AGENTS.md — Arkan Project Guide\n\n## Overview\n**Arkan** is an AI-powered academic and professional writing platform built with Next.js 15, TypeScript (strict mode), and Google Genkit. It follows Clean Architecture principles, utilizing Domain-Driven Design (DDD) to maintain strict separation between business logic and infrastructure.\n\n## Subagents — Specialist Delegation\nDelegate tasks to specialized subagents to ensure deeper focus and higher quality results. Subagent definitions are located in `.rovodev/subagents/`. Use the `invoke_subagents` tool to initiate delegation.\n\n### Delegation Matrix\n| Subagent | Primary Use Cases |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Next.js 15 AI/Server Actions** | App Router, data fetching, `use server` patterns, Genkit flows. |\n| **shadcn/ui Builder** | UI components, Radix primitives, CVA, accessibility. |\n| **Data Table/Dashboard** | Admin dashboards, TanStack Table, Recharts. |\n| **Real-time/WebSocket** | SSE, WebSockets, streaming endpoints. |\n| **State Management** | Zustand stores (`useBuilderStore`), state architecture. |\n| **Bug Hunter** | Reproducing bugs, analyzing `errors.txt`, detailed reporting. |\n| **Code Review/Best Practices** | Security audits, refactoring, code quality, consistency. |\n| **Scalability Advisor** | RAG/Qdrant optimization, API bottleneck analysis. |\n\n*Pattern:* Always delegate new feature implementation by splitting tasks: **AI Dev** (logic) + **shadcn/ui** (component) + **Server Actions** (form handling).\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Patterns\n\n### Clean Architecture (DDD)\nModules in `src/modules/` follow a standardized four-layer structure:\n1. **`domain/`**: Pure entities, repository interfaces, and Zod schemas.\n2. **`application/`**: Use cases orchestrating domain logic.\n3. **`adapters/`**: API clients, controllers, and localized Zustand stores.\n4. **`infrastructure/`**: Concrete implementations (Genkit, SQLite/Drizzle, Qdrant).\n\n### Dependency Injection (DI)\n*   **Registration**: Use `tsyringe` with `@injectable()`/`@inject()`. Register all services in `src/infrastructure/di/container.ts`.\n*   **Server-Only Logic**: Use a `typeof window === \'undefined\'` guard with `require()` inside `container.ts` to prevent client bundle contamination.\n*   **Resolution**: Use the `useService(token)` hook in React components. Avoid `new` instantiation.\n\n### AI & Genkit Flows\n*   **Implementation**: All flows must be in `src/modules/ai/infrastructure/flows/` and prefixed with `\'use server\'`.\n*   **Types & Schemas**: Use `z.enum` for strict typing; return results as `Result<T, E>` objects. Access values via `.getValue()`.\n*   **Consistency**: Use `MODEL_BY_TASK` constants. Apply `cleanAiOutput` post-processing to strip AI conversational fillers (e.g., "Sure, here is...").\n\n---\n\n## Coding Conventions\n*   **TypeScript**: Zero tolerance for `any`. Use `unknown` with narrowing.\n*   **Components**: Default to Server Components; use `\'use client\'` only when necessary.\n*   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS only. Use `cn()` for merging classes and CVA for variants.\n*   **State**: Zustand for complex client UI; TanStack Query for server state.\n*   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts` to ensure consistent status codes and telemetry.\n\n---\n\n## RAG & Infrastructure\n*   **Vector Store**: Qdrant (`arkan_vectors` collection, 768 dimensions).\n*   **Storage**: Local files via `storage/uploads/`. Protect endpoints with path-traversal checks.\n*   **i18n**: Support for English (LTR) and Arabic (RTL) via `LanguageDirectionManager`.\n\n---\n\n## Change Log\n*   **Consolidation**: Merged repetitive "Important Files" and "Environment Variables" into functional categories.\n*   **Deduplication**: Removed redundant paragraphs regarding Genkit/Ollama configuration and DI patterns scattered throughout the original file.\n*   **Structure**: Applied a logical hierarchy (Overview -> Subagents -> Architecture -> Coding -> Infrastructure).\n*   **Refinement**: Removed filler text and consolidated contradictory instructions regarding file storage and architecture patterns into definitive guidelines.\n*   **Formatting**: Standardized lists, tables, and code snippets for readability.', 'tool_response': 'Successfully replaced code in AGENTS.md:\n\n--- AGENTS.md\n+++ AGENTS.md\n@@ -43,12 +43,26 @@\n \n ---\n \n-## Coding Conventions\n-*   **TypeScript**: Zero tolerance for `any`. Use `unknown` with narrowing.\n-*   **Components**: Default to Server Components; use `\'use client\'` only when necessary.\n-*   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS only. Use `cn()` for merging classes and CVA for variants.\n-*   **State**: Zustand for complex client UI; TanStack Query for server state.\n-*   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts` to ensure consistent status codes and telemetry.\n+## Robustness & State Patterns\n+\n+### Atomic State Transformations\n+*   **Batching**: For multi-node updates (e.g., bulk context mapping), perform all transformations within a single `updateProject` callback using `targets.reduce((p, id) => p.updateSection(id, ...), project)`. This ensures atomicity and prevents race conditions.\n+*   **Existence Guards**: Implement strict `if (!project || !updateProject) return` patterns in all interaction handlers to prevent runtime crashes on unhydrated states.\n+*   **Selection Recovery**: Structural deletions must trigger callbacks to clear workspace focus (e.g., `onSelectChapter(null)`) to prevent "orphaned" UI states.\n+\n+### Defensive Programming\n+*   **Hook Compliance**: Hoist all hooks (`useMemo`, `useCallback`, `useAiActions`) to the top level, *before* any early returns. This is mandatory for Next.js 15 / React 19 stability.\n+*   **Persistence Containment**: Wrap all `updateProject` mutations and external service calls (DOCX/PPTX export, AI generation) in `try-catch` blocks with explicit user feedback (badges or toast notifications).\n+*   **ID Standardization**: Exclusively use `@/infrastructure/utils/randomId` for all domain entity identifiers. Avoid `uuidv4` or timestamp-based IDs.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Coding Conventions & UI Standards\n+*   **TypeScript**: Zero tolerance for `any`. Use `unknown` with narrowing. Use explicit `instanceof` guards for Chapter/Section entities during rendering.\n+*   **Components**: Use `React.memo` for high-frequency workspace components. Default to Server Components.\n+*   **Styling**: Technical "Intelligence Suite" aesthetic: 28px dot-grids, technical high-density labels (`text-[10px]`, `font-black`, `uppercase`), and "Stable Manifest" footers.\n+*   **State**: Zustand for document orchestration; TanStack Query for server-side metadata.\n+*   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts`.\n \n ---\n \n'}
