Payment System**: Credit-based pricing.\n  34 - **Admin Dashboard**: Comprehensive analytics, user management, and RAG monitoring.\n  35 - **State Management**: Stable client-side state with unsaved changes protection.\n  36 \n  37 ## Target Audience\n  38 - Academic Researchers, Students, Business Professionals, Educators.\n  39 \n  40 ## Business Model\n  41 - **Freemium Model**: Basic features free with premium AI tools requiring credits.\n  42 - **Credit System**: Pay-per-use for advanced AI operations.\n  43 \n  44 ## Success Metrics\n  45 - **User Engagement**: MAU, session duration, guest-to-user conversion.\n  46 - **Content Quality**: User satisfaction, RAG relevance scores.\n  47 - **Platform Growth**: New user acquisition, retention rates.\n  48 - **Revenue**: Credit purchases, subscription conversions.\n  49 \n  50 ## Technology Foundation\n  51 - **Frontend**: Next.js 15 with React 18 and TypeScript.\n  52 - **AI Engine**: Google Genkit with Gemini, Ollama (Gemma, Phi-3, Llama 3.1).\n  53 - **RAG System**:\n  54   - **Embedding Model**: Ollama with `nomic-embed-text`.\n  55   - **Vector Database**: Qdrant.\n  56 - **Backend**: SQLite (Drizzle ORM), Local File Storage, Node.js.\n  57 - **UI Framework**: Radix UI with Tailwind CSS.\n  58 - **State Management**: Zustand and React Query (TanStack).\n  59 \n  60 ## Current Status\n  61 Arkan is a stable, production-ready application with a full suite of AI writing tools and an advanced RAG system. The current focus is on increasing test coverage, refining the user experience, and monitoring performance.\n  62 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/productContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Product Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Product Vision\n   3 Arkan is the most comprehensive AI-powered writing and document generation platform, designed to empower academics, professionals, and students to create high-quality content efficiently and effectively.\n   4 \n   5 ## Product Mission\n   6 To democratize access to professional-grade writing tools by leveraging cutting-edge AI technology, making advanced content creation capabilities accessible to users regardless of their technical expertise or geographical location.\n   7 \n   8 ## Target Market & Audience\n   9 \n  10 ### Primary Segments\n  11 - **Academic Researchers & Students**\n  12 - **Business Professionals**\n  13 - **Educational Institutions**\n  14 \n  15 ### Geographic Markets\n  16 - **Primary**: Middle East & North Africa (MENA)\n  17 - **Secondary**: International English-speaking markets\n  18 \n  19 ## Core Product Features\n  20 \n  21 ### AI Writing Tools Suite (23+ Tools)\n  22 - Content Generation, Enhancement, Quality Assurance, Academic, and Technical tools.\n  23 \n  24 ### Document Generation System\n  25 - **Report Generation**: Section-based, template-driven, AI-powered content.\n  26 - **Presentation Builder**: AI slide generation with PPTX export.\n  27 - **Document Processing**: PDF analysis, handwriting recognition.\n  28 \n  29 ### **New: Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) System**\n  30 - **Semantic Search**: Find relevant information across all indexed documents using natural language.\n  31 - **Context-Aware Generation**: AI flows automatically retrieve context from the vector store to produce more accurate and informed content.\n  32 - **Knowledge Base**: Centralized knowledge base for all projects, supporting PDF, DOCX, TXT, and MD files.\n  33 - **Admin Tooling**: Document indexer, query tester, and health monitor.\n  34 \n  35 ## Product Differentiation\n  36 \n  37 ### Unique Value Propositions\n  38 1. **Comprehensive & Integrated Tool Suite**\n  39 2. **Academic & Research Focus**\n  40 3. **Cultural Adaptation (Arabic/RTL)**\n  41 4. **Professional Quality & Enterprise-Ready**\n  42 5. **Context-Aware AI**: RAG system provides grounded, accurate, and up-to-date responses.\n  43 \n  44 ### Competitive Advantages\n  45 \n  46 #### Technology Stack\n  47 - **AI Models**: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite, Ollama (Gemma 2B, Phi-3 Mini, Llama 3.1), Nomic Embed Text.\n  48 - **Vector Database**: Qdrant for high-performance semantic search.\n  49 - **Performance Optimization**: Sub-100ms search latency, advanced caching.\n  50 - **Type Safety**: Fully typed codebase with TypeScript and Zod.\n  51 \n  52 #### User Experience\n  53 - **Intuitive Interface**: Clean, modern design with excellent usability.\n  54 - **Guest Mode**: Allows users to try core features before registering.\n  55 - **State Management**: Stable, reliable state management with unsaved changes protection.\n  56 - **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance target.\n  57 \n  58 ## Business Model\n  59 \n  60 ### Revenue Streams\n  61 1. **Credit-Based System (Primary)**: Pay-per-use for AI operations.\n  62 2. **Subscription Tiers (Secondary)**\n  63 3. **Enterprise Solutions**\n  64 \n  65 ### Pricing Strategy\n  66 - Flexible credit packages for different usage levels.\n  67 - Free tier with limited monthly credits.\n  68 - Premium and Pro subscription plans.\n  69 \n  70 ## Product Development Strategy\n  71 \n  72 ### Feature Prioritization\n  73 - High Impact, Low Effort -> Priority 1\n  74 - High Impact, High Effort -> Priority 2\n  75 - User feedback and usage analytics drive prioritization.\n  76 \n  77 ### Roadmap\n  78 - **Short-term**: Enhance test coverage, UI/UX polish, performance monitoring.\n  79 - **Medium-term**: Real-time collaboration, advanced analytics, third-party integrations.\n  80 - **Long-term**: Custom AI model training, industry-specific solutions.\n  81 \n  82 ## Success Metrics & KPIs\n  83 - **User Metrics**: MAU, Retention, Session Duration, Guest-to-User Conversion.\n  84 - **Business Metrics**: MRR, CAC, LTV.\n  85 - **Product Metrics**: Tool usage, document generation volume, RAG query success rate.\n  86 - **Technical Metrics**: System uptime, AI response time, RAG latency, test coverage.\n  87 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/systemPatterns.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # System Patterns - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Architectural Patterns\n   3 \n   4 ### 1. Strict Clean Architecture (DDD)\n   5 **Purpose**: Absolute separation of concerns between business logic, orchestration, and infrastructure.\n...\n  11 ### 2. Modular AI & Schema Pattern\n  12 **Purpose**: Standardized approach for AI operations with unified data contracts.\n...\n  26 ### 5. Standardized Domain Property Pattern\n  27 **Purpose**: Enforcing type safety and predictable state management for domain entities.\n...\n  39 ## RAG & Vector Search Pattern\n  40 \n...\n  44 ### **Architecture**\n  45 1.  **Indexing Pipeline**:\n...\n  65 ### **Components**\n  66 - **Vector Store**: `src/modules/rag/infrastructure/vector-store.ts` (Factory pattern to switch between in-memory and Qdrant).\n...\n  76 ## Conversational AI Pattern (Project Consultant)\n  77 \n...\n  81 ### **Architecture**\n  82 1.  **Frontend Component (`ProjectChat.tsx`)**:\n...\n 109 ## State Management Patterns\n 110 \n 111 ### 1. Zustand Store Pattern (Client-side)\n 112 **Purpose**: Lightweight global state management for UI and session data.\n 113 - **Implementation**: `src/modules/[domain]/adapters/state/`\n 114 - **Usage**: Manages the active project, application status (`loading`, `dirty`, `saving`), and user settings. Stores are co-located with their domain.\n 115 \n 116 ### 2. Atomic State Transformation Pattern\n 117 **Purpose**: Preventing race conditions and ensuring state consistency during complex multi-node updates.\n 118 - **Implementation**: Using `targets.reduce((p, id) => p.updateSection(id, ...), project)` within a single `updateProject` callback.\n 119 - **Benefits**: Ensures that bulk operations (like updating 10 sections at once) result in a single, atomic mutation of the project manifest.\n 120 \n 121 ### 3. React Query Pattern (Server-side Cache)\n 122 **Purpose**: Server state management with caching, refetching, and synchronization.\n 123 - **Implementation**: Domain-specific hooks in `src/modules/[domain]/adapters/hooks/`.\n 124 - **Benefits**: Reduces redundant API calls, provides optimistic updates, handles background refetching. Uses centralized key factory in `src/infrastructure/api/query-keys.ts`.\n 125 \n 126 ## Robustness & Resilience Patterns\n 127 \n 128 ### 1. Unified Existence Guard Pattern\n 129 **Purpose**: Standardizing defensive checks to prevent runtime crashes on partially hydrated or null state.\n 130 - **Implementation**: Explicit `if (!project || !updateProject) return` patterns in all lifecycle and interaction handlers.\n 131 \n 132 ### 2. Neural Error Boundary Pattern\n 133 **Purpose**: Containing failures within specific UI zones (like the document renderer or AI analyst) to prevent full-page crashes.\n 134 - **Implementation**: Localized `RendererErrorBoundary` components wrapped around high-risk rendering pipelines.\n 135 \n 136 ### 3. Selection Recovery Pattern\n 137 **Purpose**: Synchronizing structural shifts with UI interaction states to prevent \"orphaned\" focuses.\n...\n 140 ## UI/UX & Architecture Patterns\n 141 \n 142 ### 1. 3-Zone Workspace Architecture (IDE Pattern)\n 143 **Purpose**: Maximizing focus and logical flow for complex document production.\n...\n 154 ### 3. Manifest Workspace Architecture\n 155 **Purpose**: Specialized layout for standalone intelligent tools (Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist).\n...\n 173 ## Error Handling Patterns\n 174 \n...\n 185 ## Security Patterns\n 186 \n...\n 203 ## Developer Experience Patterns\n 204 \n 205 ### 1. Interactive API Documentation\n 206 **Purpose**: Provide developers with a clear, interactive way to understand and test the application's API.\n...\n 216 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/techContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Technical Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Technology Stack\n   3 \n   4 ### Frontend Framework\n   5 - **Next.js 15**: React-based full-stack framework with App Router.\n   6 - **React 18**: Server and Client Components, concurrent features.\n   7 - **TypeScript**: Full type safety across the application.\n   8 - **Tailwind CSS**: Utility-first CSS framework for rapid styling.\n   9 \n  10 ### AI Integration\n  11 - **Google Genkit**: AI framework for building and deploying AI applications.\n  12 - **Generation Models**:\n  13   - Google Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite\n  14   - Ollama for local models (Gemma 2B, Phi-3 Mini, Llama 3 8B).\n  15   - **Tiered Fallback**: Automated model degradation (Llama -> Phi -> Gemma) for reliability.\n  16 - **Token Management**:\n  17   - `TokenManager`: Custom heuristic-based token counting and context truncation for local LLMs.\n  18 - **Embedding Model**:\n  19   - Ollama with `nomic-embed-text` for RAG.\n  20 - **Zod Schemas**: Type-safe validation for all AI inputs and outputs.\n  21 \n  22 ### Backend Services\n  23 - **Local Infrastructure**:\n  24   - **Database**: SQLite with Drizzle ORM for all application data.\n  25   - **Authentication**: Local JWT-based auth with bcrypt password hashing.\n  26   - **File Storage**: Local filesystem storage for user uploads (`storage/uploads`).\n  27 - **Qdrant**: High-performance vector database for the RAG system.\n  28 \n  29 ### UI Framework & Components\n  30 - **Radix UI**: Accessible, unstyled component primitives.\n  31 - **shadcn/ui**: Component library built on Radix and Tailwind.\n  32 - **Lucide Icons**: Icon library.\n  33 \n  34 ### State Management\n  35 - **Zustand**: Lightweight global client state (active project, UI state).\n  36 - **React Query (TanStack)**: Server state management, caching, and data synchronization.\n  37 - **Context APIs**: For authentication and localization.\n  38 \n  39 ## Architecture Patterns\n  40 \n  41 ### Code Organization (Clean Architecture)\n  42 ```\n  43 src/\n  44 \u251c\u2500\u2500 app/            # Next.js App Router pages and API routes\n  45 \u251c\u2500\u2500 modules/        # Domain modules (Clean Architecture / DDD)\n  46 \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 [domain]/\n  47 \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 domain/         # Entities, Repo Interfaces, Schemas\n  48 \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 application/    # Use Cases, Application Services\n  49 \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 adapters/       # Controllers, hooks, state, smart components\n  50 \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 infrastructure/ # DB/External service implementations\n  51 \u251c\u2500\u2500 components/     # Pure UI & Shared layout components\n  52 \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ui/             # shadcn/Radix primitives\n  53 \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 shared/         # Header, Footer, Providers\n  54 \u251c\u2500\u2500 hooks/          # Generic framework/utility hooks\n  55 \u2514\u2500\u2500 infrastructure/ # Cross-cutting concerns (API, DI, DB, Security)\n  56 ```\n  57 \n  58 ### RAG Architecture\n  59 - **Indexing Pipeline**: Documents -> Chunking -> Ollama Embeddings -> Qdrant Storage.\n  60 - **Retrieval Pipeline**: Query -> Embedding -> Qdrant Search -> Re-ranking -> Context.\n  61 - **Caching**: Multi-layer LRU cache for embeddings and search results.\n  62 \n  63 ### Component Patterns\n  64 - **Server & Client Components**: Optimized rendering with Next.js App Router.\n  65 - **Compound Components**: For complex UI like the report builder.\n  66 - **Custom Hooks**: Encapsulation of business logic.\n  67 \n  68 ### Data Flow Patterns\n  69 - **Server Actions**: For form submissions and mutations.\n  70 - **API Routes**: For client-server communication and external integrations.\n  71 - **Optimistic Updates**: For a smoother user experience on data mutations.\n  72 \n  73 ## Development Environment\n  74 \n  75 ### Build Tools\n  76 - **Turbopack**: Fast bundler for Next.js development.\n  77 - **ESLint & Prettier**: Code linting and formatting.\n  78 - **Jest & React Testing Library**: Unit and component testing.\n  79 \n  80 ### Local Development\n  81 - **Docker Compose**: For running local instances of Qdrant.\n  82 - **Ollama**: For running local LLMs and embedding models.\n  83 \n  84 ## Security Architecture\n  85 \n  86 ### Authentication & Authorization\n  87 - **Local Auth (SQLite)**: Secure local authentication with JWT and bcrypt.\n  88 - **Injectable Auth Services**: `IPasswordService` and `ITokenService` for flexible implementation.\n  89 - **Cookie-Based Sessions**: Automated session management via `ICookieService`.\n  90 - **Middleware**: Route protection for authenticated and admin-only routes.\n  91 - **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**: 'admin' vs 'user' roles enforced on the server.\n  92 - **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Strict isolation of heavy AI infrastructure (Genkit, Express) from the client bundle using relocated constants and runtime guards.\n  93 \n  94 ### Data Security\n  95 - **Firestore Rules**: Database-level security rules.\n  96 - **Input Validation**: Zod schemas for all API inputs and AI flows.\n  97 - **Image Proxy**: Whitelisted domains for secure image fetching.\n  98 \n  99 ## Performance Optimization\n 100 \n 101 ### Frontend Performance\n 102 - **Code Splitting**: Automatic per-route code splitting.\n 103 - **Next.js Image Optimization**: Lazy loading and optimized image formats.\n 104 - **React Server Components**: Reduced client-side JavaScript.\n 105 - **Client-side Caching**: Using React Query and Zustand to cache data and state.\n 106 \n 107 ### Backend Performance\n 108 - **RAG Caching**: Multi-layer caching for embeddings and search results reduces latency.\n 109 - **Qdrant Indexing**: HNSW indexing for fast vector search.\n 110 - **Firestore Indexing**: Custom indexes for efficient database queries.\n 111 - **Serverless Functions**: Scalable, on-demand backend logic.\n 112 \n 113 ## Deployment & Infrastructure\n 114 \n 115 ### Hosting\n 116 - **Contabo Hosting**: For deploying the Next.js frontend.\n 117 - **PostgreSQL**: For backend services (Auth, Firestore, Functions).\n 118 - **Self-hosted / openrouter.ai**: For running Qdrant and Ollama services.\n 119 \n 120 ### Environment Management\n 121 - **Environment Variables**: Centralized and validated configuration (`src/lib/config.ts`).\n 122 - `.env.example`: Template for easy setup.\n 123 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/activeContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Active Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Recently Completed\n   3 - **Clean Architecture Overhaul**: The project has reached a \"Gold Standard\" architectural state. All domain logic, state (Zustand), hooks, and smart components have been relocated into a self-contained module hierarchy (`src/modules/*`).\n   4 - **Complete Firebase Client Removal**: All client-side Firebase SDK dependencies have been removed. Authentication is now strictly local (SQLite backend + Cookie management), and the vector store is decoupled from Firestore persistence.\n   5 - **Unified AI Flow Ecosystem**: 40+ Genkit flows have been categorized and standardized with a unified schema registry, ensuring 100% type safety and zero circular dependencies.\n   6 - **Performance Optimization Pass**: High-frequency components (Report Builder) now utilize atomic Zustand selectors and `React.memo` to minimize virtual DOM overhead.\n   7 - **DI for React**: Introduced a standardized `useService(token)` pattern for resolving dependencies within the React lifecycle.\n   8 - **Zone Tabs Architecture Implementation**: Successfully transitioned the main `ReportModeGenerator` to a professional 3-zone architecture (Top/Left/Center/Right).\n   9 - **Production Grade UI Overhaul**: Modernized all critical document production workflows, including Blueprinting (TOC), Construction (Build), and Production (Export) manifests.\n  10 - **Visual Identity Synchronization**: Unified the brand aesthetic across the Home Page, Global Header, and interactive Cover Page editor.\n  11 - **Writing Tools Modernization**: Completed a high-fidelity overhaul of flagship specialist tools (**Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, Document Writer, Blueprint, Quiz, UI Description, Idea Generator, Lecture Generator, Session Plan, Assignments Solver**), transitioning them to the Manifest Workspace layout.\n  12 - **Platform-Wide Aesthetic Unification**: Standardized typography (`serif 15px`), layout grids, and interactive patterns across all core production surfaces.\n  13 - **Admin Console Modernization**: Transitioned the internal management suite to a professional 3-zone layout with technical HUD navigation and manifest-style management consoles for core system operations.\n  14 - **AI Module Resilience Enhancement**: Implemented tiered model fallback (Llama 3 \u2192 Phi-3 \u2192 Gemma 2B) and proactive request timeouts to ensure system stability in 8GB RAM environments.\n  15 - **Domain Entity Property Pattern Standardization**: Standardized all domain entities on the `toProperties()`, `toStateObject()`, and `withProps()` pattern for type-safe serialization and cloning.\n  16 - **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Successfully decoupled heavy AI SDK dependencies from the client bundle by relocating constants and implementing strict runtime guards.\n  17 - **Robustness Refactoring & State Hardening**: Completed a massive hardening pass across 15+ AI Builder components. Resolved Next.js 15 hook violations, implemented atomic state transformations, and standardized defensive programming guards (`if (!project) return`) and error containment (`try-catch`) project-wide.\n  18 - **Structural Integrity & Recovery**: Standardized the `randomId()` utility and implemented automated \"Selection Recovery\" to prevent orphaned UI states during structural deletions.\n  19 - **Neural Rendering Safety**: Introduced localized Error Boundaries for the document canvas and reinforced snapshot validation for the version comparison engine.\n  20 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/recentUpdates.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Recent Updates - Arkan Memory Bank\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: March 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## April 2026 Updates\n   5 \n   6 ### **Robustness Refactoring & State Hardening**\n   7 **Date**: April 2026\n   8 **Summary**: Completed a massive hardening pass across the AI Builder orchestration layer to ensure production-grade stability and Next.js 15 compliance.\n   9 \n  10 - **Next.js 15 Hook Compliance**: Resolved critical \"Rules of Hooks\" violations by standardizing hook placement above early returns in all HUD components.\n  11 - **Defensive Programming Standards**: Implemented universal existence guards (`if (!project) return`) and persistence containment (`try-catch`) around all domain mutations and external service calls.\n  12 - **Atomic State Transformations**: Transitioned complex multi-node operations (Context Mapping, Guideline Editing, Structural Reordering) to single-pass atomic reductions, eliminating race conditions.\n  13 - **Structural Integrity & Recovery**: Standardized the `randomId()` utility project-wide and implemented \"Selection Recovery\" sweeps to clear orphaned UI states after structural deletions.\n  14 - **Neural Rendering Safety**: Introduced a dedicated Error Boundary for the document canvas and integrated snapshot validation passes for the version comparison engine.\n  15 \n  16 ## March 2026 Updates\n  17 \n  18 ### **AI Resilience & Domain Hardening**\n  19 **Date**: Late March 2026\n  20 \n  21 - **Tiered Fallback Logic**: Implemented automated model degradation (Llama 3 \u2192 Phi-3 \u2192 Gemma 2B) to ensure 8GB RAM stability.\n  22 - **Standardized Entity Pattern**: Unified all domain entities on the `toProperties()` and `withProps()` pattern, enforcing strict type safety and deep immutability.\n  23 - **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Resolved critical bundling errors by isolating heavy server-side AI SDKs from the browser chunking context.\n  24 - **Token-Aware Truncation**: Added proactive context management to prevent LLM context window overflows during RAG operations.\n  25 \n  26 ### **Full Architectural Hardening & Firebase Decommissioning**\n  27 **Date**: March 2026\n  28 **Summary**: Completed a massive refactor to align the entire project with strict Clean Architecture (DDD) principles.\n  29 \n  30 - **Module-Centric Organization**: Relocated all Hooks, Smart Components, and Zustand Stores into their respective domain modules (`users`, `projects`, `ai`, `ai-content`, `billing`, `rag`, `templates`, `admin`).\n  31 - **Legacy Cleanup**: Completely removed `src/lib` and `src/hooks/data` / `src/hooks/core` directories.\n  32 - **AI Ecosystem Refinement**: Categorized 40+ AI flows and unified all tool/flow schemas into a single infrastructure source of truth.\n  33 - **Local Auth Completion**: Fully removed Firebase Client SDK logic. Implemented injectable `CookieService`, `SessionService`, `PasswordService`, and `TokenService`.\n  34 - **Infrastructure Purity**: Decoupled RAG Vector Store and Domain Entities from Firebase types, utilizing native JS types and functional injection for complex parsing logic.\n  35 - **React Performance**: Optimized store access with atomic selectors and implemented memoization for the Report Builder sub-components.\n  36 \n  37 ### **Zone Tabs Layout & Production UI Overhaul**\n  38 **Date**: March 2026\n  39 **Summary**: Modernized the core document production workspace and unified the brand identity across the platform.\n  40 \n  41 - **3-Zone Architecture**: Transitioned the main generator to a professional 3-column \"IDE Pattern\" with persistent Top Identity, Left Setup, Center Document, and Right AI Context zones.\n  42 - **Manifest Interaction Model**: Redesigned all multi-step processes (Build, Export, Library) into technical manifests with activity-ready pulsing headers and data-dense bodies.\n  43 - **Professional Sidebar Density**: Standardized sidebar aesthetics with bold uppercase tracking and context-first hierarchies (e.g., reordering Context -> Prompt -> Controls).\n  44 - **Contextual HUDs**: Implemented semi-transparent floating glass-morphism HUDs for secondary utilities like Zoom and Syntax Guides.\n  45 - **Visual Identity Synchronization**: Unified the brand aesthetic across the Home Page, Global Header, and interactive Cover Page editor with high-fidelity textures and typography.\n  46 - **Writing Tools Overhaul**: Completed a high-fidelity modernization of flagship specialist tools (**Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, Document Writer, Blueprint, Quiz, UI Description, Idea Generator, Lecture Generator, Session Plan, Assignments Solver**), transitioning them to the Manifest Workspace layout with technical setup panels and high-depth results canvases.\n  47 - **Admin Console Modernization**: Replaced the legacy admin interface with a professional 3-zone architecture, featuring technical HUD navigation, a sticky system status header, and manifest-style management consoles for Users, Payments, Templates, and RAG Ingestion.\n  48 \n  49 ## January 2026 Updates\n  50 \n  51 ### **RAG System & Production Readiness**\n  52 **Date**: January 2026\n  53 **Impact**: Critical - Core functionality enhancement\n  54 **Status**: \u2705 Completed\n  55 \n  56 **Features & Fixes**:\n  57 1. **Full RAG System Implementation**\n  58    - Integrated **Qdrant** as the production-ready vector database.\n  59    - Utilized **Ollama** with `nomic-embed-text` model for generating embeddings.\n  60    - Implemented a complete indexing pipeline (`indexer.ts`) for processing and vectorizing documents.\n  61    - Built a robust retrieval pipeline (`retrieval.ts`) with advanced filtering.\n  62 \n  63 2. **Admin RAG Tooling**\n  64    - Created a **Document Indexer** page for admins to upload and manage knowledge base files (PDF, DOCX, TXT).\n  65    - Developed a **RAG Query Tester** for real-time search testing with configurable parameters (topK, minScore, reranking).\n  66    - Added a **RAG Health Monitor** to check the status of Qdrant and Ollama services.\n  67 \n  68 3. **Advanced RAG Features**\n  69    - Implemented a multi-layer **caching system** for embeddings and search results, improving repeated query latency by over 90%.\n  70    - Added multiple **re-ranking strategies** (Hybrid, Cross-Encoder, BM25) to enhance search result quality.\n  71 \n  72 4. **Critical Configuration Fixes**\n  73    - Enabled strict mode for TypeScript and ESLint in `next.config.ts` to catch errors at build time.\n  74    - Centralized all environment variables into `src/lib/config.ts` with Zod validation.\n  75    - Removed all hardcoded IP addresses and configuration values.\n  76 \n  77 5. **State Management Overhaul**\n  78    - Refactored `useBuilderStore` to be more stable and client-centric.\n  79    - Implemented a clear status system (`loading`, `idle`, `dirty`, `saving`).\n  80    - Added a `useBeforeUnload` hook to prevent accidental loss of unsaved changes.\n  81    - Improved editor synchronization logic to be more reliable.\n  82 \n  83 6. **Guest Mode & UI Stability**\n  84    - Implemented a \"Continue as Guest\" feature for new users.\n  85    - Guest projects are persisted locally in IndexedDB.\n  86    - Disabled all credit-based and cloud-save features for guests.\n  87    - Stabilized the main `Header` component to prevent hydration mismatch errors.\n  88 \n  89 7. **Comprehensive Payment Management**\n  90    - Overhauled the admin settings page to allow full CRUD management of all payment methods (e-wallets, banks, etc.).\n  91    - Created a flexible data structure to support diverse payment types.\n  92    - Simplified the user-facing credit purchase dialog to use a dynamic credit amount slider instead of fixed plans.\n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/progress.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Progress Report - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: March 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## Development Milestones\n   5 \n   6 ### Phase 1: Foundation (Completed - Q3 2024)\n   7 \u2705 **Core Infrastructure**\n   8 \u2705 **Authentication System**\n   9 \u2705 **Initial AI Integration**\n  10 \n  11 ### Phase 2: Core Features (Completed - Q4 2024)\n  12 \u2705 **AI Writing Tools Suite** (23+ tools)\n  13 \u2705 **Document Generation System** (DOCX, PPTX)\n  14 \u2705 **User Management** (Admin Dashboard, RBAC)\n  15 \n  16 ### Phase 3: Advanced Features (Completed - Q4 2024)\n  17 \u2705 **Payment System** (Credit-based)\n  18 \u2705 **Multi-language Support** (EN/AR with RTL)\n  19 \u2705 **Admin Dashboard** (Analytics, User/Payment Management)\n  20 \n  21 ### Phase 4: Quality & Reliability (Completed - December 2024)\n  22 \u2705 **Document Export Reliability**: Comprehensive DOCX/PPTX export bug fixes.\n  23 \u2705 **Agent Lab Optimization**: SQLite backend, caching, and performance tuning.\n  24 \u2705 **Comprehensive Payment Management**: Full admin UI for all payment methods.\n  25 \n  26 ### Phase 5: RAG System & Production Readiness (Completed - January 2026)\n  27 \u2705 **RAG System Implementation**: Qdrant vector store, Ollama embedding models.\n  28 \u2705 **Admin RAG Tooling**: Document indexer, real-time query tester, health monitor.\n  29 \u2705 **Advanced RAG Features**: Multi-layer caching and hybrid re-ranking.\n  30 \u2705 **Critical Configuration Fixes**: Enabled strict modes, validated environment variables.\n  31 \u2705 **State Management Overhaul**: Implemented stable, client-side first state management with unsaved changes protection.\n  32 \u2705 **Guest Mode**: Implemented \"Continue as Guest\" feature with local persistence.\n  33 \n  34 ### Phase 6: Hardening & Expansion (Completed - March 2026)\n  35 \u2705 **API Documentation System**: Interactive, self-documenting API portal.\n  36 \u2705 **AI Project Consultant Chat**: In-app conversational AI to assist with project development.\n  37 \u2705 **Architectural Hardening**: Reached 100% Clean Architecture (DDD) compliance.\n  38 \u2705 **Firebase Client Decommissioning**: Fully migrated to local SQLite/Cookie-based auth and removed client-side SDKs.\n  39 \u2705 **Local File Storage**: Replaced Firebase Cloud Storage with local filesystem storage.\n  40 \u2705 **AI Infrastructure Refinement**: Categorized flows and unified tool schemas.\n  41 \u2705 **Zone Tabs Layout Implementation**: Modernized the main generator with a persistent 3-zone architecture.\n  42 \u2705 **Integrated Global AI Settings**: Moved behavioral rules and parameters to contextual sidebars.\n  43 \u2705 **Manifest Interaction Model**: Standardized multi-step operations into production-grade manifest dialogs.\n  44 \u2705 **Writing Tools Overhaul**: Completed a high-fidelity overhaul of flagship specialist tools (**Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, Document Writer, Blueprint, Quiz, UI Description, Idea Generator, Lecture Generator, Session Plan, Assignments Solver**), transitioning them to the Manifest Workspace layout.\n  45 \u2705 **Admin Console Modernization**: Replaced the legacy admin interface with a professional 3-zone architecture and manifest-style management consoles for Users, Payments, Templates, and Document Indexing.\n  46 \n  47 ### Phase 7: Production Stability & Robustness (Completed - April 2026)\n  48 \u2705 **Robustness Refactoring**: Hardened all 15+ orchestration HUDs with defensive programming and existence guards.\n  49 \u2705 **Next.js 15 Compliance**: Resolved Rules of Hooks violations and standardized hook placement across the builder.\n  50 \u2705 **Atomic State Hardening**: Implemented atomic transformations for complex multi-node operations.\n  51 \u2705 **Error Containment**: Introduced localized Error Boundaries and persistence containment (`try-catch`) project-wide.\n  52 \u2705 **Structural Integrity**: Standardized the `randomId()` utility and selection recovery logic.\n  53 \n  54 ### Phase 8: Scaling & Optimization (Current Focus)\n  55 \u2705 **AI Resilience Enhancement**: Implemented tiered model fallback and request timeouts for 8GB RAM stability.\n  56 \u2705 **Domain Entity Standardization**: Unified all domain entities on the `toProperties()` and `withProps()` pattern.\n  57 \u2705 **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Resolved critical bundling errors by isolating heavy AI SDKs from the browser.\n  58 - \ud83d\udd04 **Test Coverage Expansion**: Increase unit and integration test coverage to 40%+.\n  59 - \ud83d\udd04 **Performance Monitoring**: Implement real-time monitoring.\n  60 - \ud83d\udd04 **RAG Retrieval Optimization**: Implement hybrid search and reranking improvements.\n  61 - \ud83d\udd04 **UI Performance**: Further optimize React rendering for the editor.\n  62 - \ud83d\udd04 **Mobile Experience Refinement**: Optimize the 3-zone architecture for smaller touch devices.\n  63 \n  64 \n  65 ## Feature Completion Status\n  66 \n  67 ### Writing Tools (23/23 - 100% Complete)\n  68 \u2705 All core writing tools are operational.\n  69 \n  70 ### Document Features (100% Complete)\n  71 \u2705 Report Generation, Presentation Builder, Document Export.\n  72 \n  73 ### RAG System (100% Complete)\n  74 \u2705 Semantic Search, Context-Aware Generation, Knowledge Base.\n  75 \n  76 ### Platform Features (100% Complete)\n  77 \u2705 User Authentication, Payment Processing, Multi-language Support, Admin Dashboard.\n  78 \u2705 **AI Project Consultant Chat**: In-app conversational AI to assist with project development.\n  79 \n  80 ### Developer Experience (New)\n  81 \u2705 **Interactive API Documentation**: A comprehensive, self-documenting portal for all API endpoints.\n  82 \n  83 ## Technical Achievements\n  84 \n  85 ### Architecture Excellence\n  86 - \u2705 **Modular Design** & **Type Safety**\n  87 - \u2705 **RAG Architecture**: Scalable pipeline for indexing and retrieval.\n  88 - \u2705 **State Management**: Robust and predictable client-side state.\n  89 \n  90 ### Code Quality Metrics\n  91 - **Test Coverage**: ~20% (focus for next phase).\n  92 - **TypeScript Coverage**: 99%+ type safety.\n  93 - **ESLint Compliance**: Zero linting errors in production code.\n  94 - **Performance Score**: 90+ Lighthouse score.\n  95 \n  96 ## User Adoption Metrics\n  97 \n  98 ### Current Statistics (January 2026)\n  99 - **Total Users**: 2,500+ (stable)\n 100 - **Monthly Active Users**: 1,200+\n 101 - **User Retention**: 65% (30-day retention rate)\n 102 \n 103 ## Business Metrics\n 104 \n 105 ### Revenue Performance\n 106 - **Monthly Recurring Revenue**: $8,500\n 107 - **Conversion Rate**: 12% (free to paid)\n 108 \n 109 ## Next Steps\n 110 \n 111 ### Phase 6: Hardening & Expansion (Continued)\n 112 - \ud83d\udd04 **Test Coverage Expansion**: Increase unit and integration test coverage to 40%+.\n 113 - \ud83d\udd04 **UI/UX Refinement**: Polish all user-facing interfaces.\n 114 - \ud83d\udd04 **Performance Monitoring**: Implement real-time monitoring.\n 115 - \ud83d\udd04 **Collaboration Features**: Begin development of team-based features.\n 116 \n 117 The Arkan project has successfully transitioned from a feature-complete platform to a production-ready, stable, and high-performance system with advanced RAG capabilities. The foundation is solid for continued growth and expansion.\n 118 \n````"], "tool_call_id": "pyd_ai_ad7b8a136e5147e38dd57dbaf4878c6f", "metadata": null, "timestamp": "2026-04-05T08:20:51.193538+00:00", "part_kind": "tool-return"}
